Source: audiocpp-tts
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Grigory Tuboltsev <gtubolcev@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake (>= 3.20), pkgconf,
 libvulkan-dev, glslc, spirv-headers
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/0xShug0/audio.cpp
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libaudiocpp-tts
Architecture: amd64
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: libespeak-ng1, espeak-ng-data, mesa-vulkan-drivers
Description: audio.cpp speech models on ggml - private copy for linux-tts
 audio.cpp runs speech, music and audio models (Piper, Kokoro, Supertonic,
 Pocket TTS and many more) on ggml, on the processor or through Vulkan on
 the graphics card. This is its C library with ggml and the backends: one
 CPU backend per instruction set level, picked at run time, and Vulkan.
 .
 It is installed in /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts/audiocpp for the speech
 module sd_audiocpp of the linux-tts PPA. Piper voices need espeak-ng.

Package: libaudiocpp-tts-dev
Architecture: amd64
Section: libdevel
Depends: libaudiocpp-tts (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: audio.cpp speech models on ggml - private copy (headers)
 audio.cpp runs speech, music and audio models on ggml.
 .
 This package has the C API header in /usr/include/linux-tts and
 audiocpp.pc in /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts/pkgconfig; set
 PKG_CONFIG_PATH to use it, and a RUNPATH to run.
